// Minimal modal-dialog client, for regression-testing input on Android dialogs
// under fydroid.
//
// Deliberately NOT in PRODUCT_PACKAGES — it is a developer tool, not part of the
// image. Build and install it explicitly:
//
//   m FydroidDialogTest
//   push the apk and `pm install -r` it inside the container
//
// Drive it with (each mode logs every touch/key it receives, tag FydroidDialogTest):
//   am start -n io.fydeos.dialogtest/.MainActivity -e mode perm      # POST_NOTIFICATIONS prompt
//   am start -n io.fydeos.dialogtest/.MainActivity -e mode alert     # AlertDialog
//   am start -n io.fydeos.dialogtest/.MainActivity -e mode dialogact # dialog-themed activity
// The dialog activity's "Use" buttons start a full-screen page (same task or a new
// task) while the dialog stays up: the shape of the TapTap SDK login in Phigros.
//
// Hardware-key typing: the main screen has a text, a password and an
// autocorrect field, and WebActivity has the same three as WebView inputs; each
// logs its value on every change (tag FydroidDialogTest).
//   am start -n io.fydeos.dialogtest/.WebActivity                      # WebView fields
//   am start -n io.fydeos.dialogtest/.MainActivity -e mode translucentweb
//     # translucent WebView activity over MainActivity in the same task
// Run modes from a cold start (am force-stop first).
android_app {
    name: "FydroidDialogTest",
    srcs: ["src/**/*.java"],
    sdk_version: "current",
    dex_preopt: {
        enabled: false,
    },
}
